## Step 4: Identify Best Unexplored Direction

Looking at the Pareto front, the most promising balanced region is around **E~500-600, PF~0.33-0.36**. The condition 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1 (E=520, PF=0.36) is the best confirmed single-run balanced point on the Pareto front.

**Key observations from the data:**
- Lower polymer_wt (17–17.5) tends to give higher PF
- Cold bath (5°C) with N2 and moderate wait times gives good E
- bath_temp=15°C with 17.5 wt% polymer gives PF~0.32-0.36
- The 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 condition shows promise but high run-to-run variability

**Unexplored promising region**: 17.5 wt% polymer, bath_temp=10-15°C, moderate wait time ~60-90s, N2=True, mixing_temp=65°C. The condition **17p5-10deg-90s-N2** (mixing_temp=65, bath_temp=10, pullcast_speed=8, wait=90s, nips=1800s) gave E=442, PF=0.31 — decent but not Pareto-optimal.

**New exploration target**: Try to push toward higher E while maintaining PF≥0.33. The data suggests bath_temp=5°C tends to give higher E (e.g., 17-5deg run2: E=547, PF=0.31; 17p5-10deg-15s run1: E=709, PF=0.28). But PF tends to be lower at bath_temp=5°C.

A promising unexplored combination: **polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=10°C, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=30s, N2=True, mixing_temp=65°C, pullcast_speed=10, nips_bath_wait_time=1800s**. This is close to the 17p5-10deg-15s condition but with slightly longer wait (30s vs 15s) and faster pullcast. The 15s wait gave high E but variable PF (0.28-0.33). A 30s wait at bath_temp=10°C might stabilize toward higher PF while maintaining good E.

